 "disclosure": "Two harness-only bugs in the NEGATIVE early-decide helper (the extra actor that decides early), found by its first runs and fixed one line each with new-inode writes, then that mode rerun on the fixed harness (4/0): (1) `status | grep -q` under pipefail (SIGPIPE) never matched; (2) the config glob matched fx*.db.liveness.json first. Evidence of both failed runs kept in attempt-history/composition-runs/. frozen-harness-v2/v3.sha256 record the harness bytes. The driver, evaluator, lane, engine, prep and inputs never changed after the freeze; positive and neg-no-receiver ran on harness v1, whose paths for those modes are unchanged. Because a frozen file (inject-test.sh) changed after the freeze, the claim is labelled by the generator, not by me."
